# Historical preservation

This repository is both software and a research artifact.

When a change could alter numerical results, training behavior, evaluation semantics, timing, memory layout, routing, initialization, or randomization:

1. identify the exact historical path;
2. add or update a test that captures current behavior when feasible;
3. document suspected defects in `docs/KNOWN_ISSUES.md` before repairing them;
4. state whether the change can affect published results;
5. separate compatibility/reproduction behavior from corrected/modern behavior;
6. never silently replace historical benchmark numbers with new measurements.

Prefer additive modernization layers over destructive rewrites until reproduction is established.
